searchData={"items":[{"type":"module","title":"MedRTC","doc":"WebRTC preview and recording over independent lifetimes.","ref":"MedRTC.html"},{"type":"module","title":"MedRTC.Preview","doc":"One replaceable, send-only WebRTC peer for an Opus preview. The caller owns\nthe peer and receives its ExWebRTC state changes. Capture has its own lifetime.","ref":"MedRTC.Preview.html"},{"type":"type","title":"MedRTC.Preview.t/0","doc":"","ref":"MedRTC.Preview.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"function","title":"MedRTC.Preview.answer/1","doc":"Answers a receive-only audio offer containing the browser's ICE candidates.","ref":"MedRTC.Preview.html#answer/1"},{"type":"function","title":"MedRTC.Preview.close/1","doc":"","ref":"MedRTC.Preview.html#close/1"},{"type":"function","title":"MedRTC.Preview.send_opus/3","doc":"Sends one 20 ms Opus frame. Frame indices are relative to the acquisition.","ref":"MedRTC.Preview.html#send_opus/3"},{"type":"module","title":"MedRTC.WavCapture","doc":"Replays a finite mono PCM16 WAV and its prepared 20 ms Opus preview.\nRecording integrity describes the retained file payload. Each final artifact\nis identified by its canonical WAV digest and its decoded PCM digest.","ref":"MedRTC.WavCapture.html"},{"type":"type","title":"MedRTC.WavCapture.parsed_wav/0","doc":"","ref":"MedRTC.WavCapture.html#t:parsed_wav/0"},{"type":"function","title":"MedRTC.WavCapture.encode_pcm16_wav/2","doc":"Encodes raw 16-bit signed little-endian mono PCM into a standard RIFF/WAVE\nbinary.","ref":"MedRTC.WavCapture.html#encode_pcm16_wav/2"},{"type":"function","title":"MedRTC.WavCapture.parse_wav/1","doc":"Parses an uncompressed PCM WAV binary (handling arbitrary RIFF chunks before\n`fmt ` and `data`, as emitted by clinical recorders and PhysioNet CirCor).","ref":"MedRTC.WavCapture.html#parse_wav/1"},{"type":"function","title":"MedRTC.WavCapture.record/4","doc":"Paces a verified WAV fixture and atomically finalizes its original PCM in\na playable WAV. The paired Ogg file contains 20 ms Opus frames derived from\nthe same input. Preview is best-effort and can stall or fail independently.\n\nRun this operation in the acquisition task. Supply `:on_preview_frame`\nto receive `(frame_index, opus_payload)` from the preview worker.","ref":"MedRTC.WavCapture.html#record/4"},{"type":"module","title":"MedWeb","doc":"Reusable Phoenix signaling contract (`MedWeb.Signaling`) and shipped browser\n`RTCPeerConnection` hook assets for MedEx live sessions.","ref":"MedWeb.html"},{"type":"module","title":"MedWeb.Signaling","doc":"Locates the browser hook in a source child or the released SDK.","ref":"MedWeb.Signaling.html"},{"type":"function","title":"MedWeb.Signaling.hook_asset_full_path/0","doc":"","ref":"MedWeb.Signaling.html#hook_asset_full_path/0"},{"type":"extras","title":"Overview","doc":"# MedEx\nMedEx provides two source projects, `core/med_rtc` for replay and WebRTC peers, and `core/med_web` for browser signaling. Fabric owns clinical decisions. Consumers depend on one commit-pinned Git SDK named `:med_ex`.\n\nOn Ubuntu 26.04 install Git, curl, tar, build-essential, shasum and uv. Activate the exact Erlang and Elixir in .tool-versions through asdf or mise. Run `./onboard.sh --fixture`, `mix ci` and `mix weld.verify`.\n\n`MedRTC.WavCapture.record/4` takes WAV input, a prepared Opus preview, an existing output directory and acquisition options. The result identifies the complete WAV and its decoded PCM separately. Each peer is owned by its channel. The browser host supplies the socket path, topic and control selectors to `createMedExHook`. See the Fabric exam for the released integration.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  WAV --> Capture --> ImmutableWAV\n  Capture --> Preview --> Peer --> Browser\n```","ref":"readme.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Changelog","doc":"# Changelog\n\nAll notable changes to the `med_ex` poncho workspace will be documented in this file.\n\n## [0.1.0] - 2026-11-22","ref":"changelog.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Added - Changelog","doc":"- Initialized the `med_ex` non-umbrella Elixir poncho workspace with Blitz and Weld orchestration.\n- Added architecture documentation and skeleton packages under `core/` (`med_core`, `med_rtc`, `med_adapters`, `med_web`) and `apps/` (`med_pulse`).\n- Configured Credo, Dialyxir, ExDoc, custom SVG branding assets, and per-package metadata across every child Mix project.","ref":"changelog.html#added"},{"type":"extras","title":"License","doc":"MIT License\n\nCopyright (c) 2026 nshkrdotcom\n\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\nof this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\nin the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\nto use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\ncopies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\nfurnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\ncopies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\nIMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\nFITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\nAUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\nLIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\nOUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\nSOFTWARE.","ref":"license.html"}],"proglang":"elixir","content_type":"text/markdown","producer":{"name":"ex_doc","version":"0.40.5"}}